;; stdlib/shankpit/citizen_actor_rules.prn -- what a citizen in MODE_ZOMBIES does with its body.
;;
;; Founder real-time: "lets make the citizens in zombie mode more dynamic have them be able to jump
;; ... merge player physics with citizen physics ... allow them to jump crouch slide and slide jump
;; also wield weapons ... wire up heuristics mixed with a parena hand written llm".
;;
;; The split this file draws, and why:
;;   * PHYSICS is not re-invented here. A citizen is a real PlayerState and already runs the
;;     player's own update_entity / accelerate / apply_friction / crouch-slide / wall-ride path
;;     (local_game.h). "Merging" the two means a citizen now writes the SAME input fields a human
;;     writes -- in_jump, crouching, in_shoot, current_weapon -- instead of only in_fwd and yaw. So
;;     the numbers below are the inputs the shared physics consumes, in the shared units (vy in
;;     milli of a unit/tick, speeds in milli), never a second movement system.
;;   * DECIDING is what this file owns, and it is deliberately two opinions blended:
;;       1. HAND-WRITTEN HEURISTICS (citizen-heuristic-score): one explainable scorer per action,
;;          the kind of if-ladder a designer can read and retune.
;;       2. A HAND-WRITTEN POLICY (citizen-policy-aggression): a fixed-point perceptron -- six
;;          features, six hand-picked weights, no training, no clock, no state. It is a policy
;;          NETWORK the way a shader is a program: small, inspectable, and wrong in ways you can
;;          point at. This is NOT a language model and this file does not pretend otherwise: a real
;;          LLM needs weights that are trained and megabytes of file, neither of which belongs in a
;;          pure-total-I32 decision library. What the founder asked for that IS honest to build here
;;          is "heuristics mixed with a learned-shaped scorer", and that is exactly this pair.
;;       citizen-blended-score mixes them per action: heuristics decide, the policy leans
;;       (+/- bias scaled by how aggressive it feels right now), and citizen-pick is the argmax.
;;   * FIGHT PLAN. Moving and shooting is not a plan, so three scorers answer the questions a
;;     cornered body actually asks: DODGE when a claw is already inside its reach, TAKE COVER (drop
;;     the profile, give ground, keep it in front) when hurt but not yet in reach, and RETREAT when
;;     badly hurt -- turn and break for distance. Which WAY is clear is geometry, and geometry is the
;;     host's (it owns the walls and the bodies); how hurt is too hurt, how close is a claw, and how
;;     long a dodge or a retreat commits are here, because they are design numbers.
;;
;; Everything is I32, total (no division by a zero a caller can pass), no RNG, no clock, no state:
;; the host owns the tick, the cooldowns and the bodies. Retune here and
;; `make regen-citizen-actor-rules`.
(module shankpit/citizen-actor-rules)
(export citizen-jump-vy-milli citizen-jump-cooldown-ms citizen-crouch-speed-milli
        citizen-slide-speed-milli citizen-slide-min-ms citizen-slide-max-ms
        citizen-slide-jump-boost-milli citizen-slide-jump-window-ms
        citizen-wield-range-milli citizen-fire-range-milli citizen-fire-cooldown-ms
        citizen-claw-reach-milli citizen-dodge-ms citizen-cover-health-pm citizen-cover-ms
        citizen-cover-backpedal-milli citizen-retreat-health-pm citizen-retreat-ms
        citizen-heuristic-score citizen-policy-aggression citizen-blended-score citizen-pick)

;; ---- action ids (the C side's CitizenActor enum, one contract) -------------------------------
;; 0 idle  1 walk  2 run  3 jump  4 crouch  5 slide  6 slide-jump  7 shoot  8 reload
;; 9 dodge  10 take-cover  11 retreat

(defn citizen-clamp [(lo : I32) (hi : I32) (x : I32)] : I32
  (if (< x lo) lo (if (> x hi) hi x)))

;; ---- physics inputs, in the engine's own units -----------------------------------------------
;; JUMP_FORCE is 0.95 units/tick in physics.h; stated here in milli so the shared jump path gets a
;; number a mod can own without touching the player's own jump. 950 milli = today's human jump: a
;; citizen that jumps today jumps exactly as high as a person, which is what "merged physics" means.
(defn citizen-jump-vy-milli [] : I32 950)

;; Long enough that a cornered citizen cannot pogo out of trouble, short enough that a chase over a
;; fence looks alive. The human jump has no cooldown; an actor needs one or it hops every tick.
(defn citizen-jump-cooldown-ms [] : I32 900)

;; CROUCH_SPEED (physics.h) is 0.35 -- the human crouch-walk cap. Same number, same feel.
(defn citizen-crouch-speed-milli [] : I32 350)

;; The speed at which the engine's own crouch-slide drag (SLIDE_FRICTION) takes over: physics.h
;; switches at 0.75 units/tick. Below this a crouch is just a crouch, so a slide is never asked for.
(defn citizen-slide-speed-milli [] : I32 750)

(defn citizen-slide-min-ms [] : I32 350)
(defn citizen-slide-max-ms [] : I32 1400)

;; A slide jump is the founder's own move: leave a slide with the slide's momentum plus a kick.
;; 200 milli on top of the shared 950 is a visible hop, not flight.
(defn citizen-slide-jump-boost-milli [] : I32 200)
(defn citizen-slide-jump-window-ms [] : I32 250)

;; A citizen notices a weapon-worthy problem before it is on top of it, and shoots from further
;; than it draws. 14 m is inside the eye-line of the maps' streets.
(defn citizen-wield-range-milli [] : I32 12000)
(defn citizen-fire-range-milli [] : I32 14000)
(defn citizen-fire-cooldown-ms [] : I32 260)

;; ---- the fight plan's own numbers ----------------------------------------------------------
;; A claw is in reach at 3.2 m (witness_ai.c's WAI_ZOMBIE_CLAW_REACH, minus a body radius). Inside
;; 2.6 m a standing body is already being hit, so the plan is a sidestep, not a shot.
(defn citizen-claw-reach-milli [] : I32 2600)

;; A dodge is a commitment like a slide: a side-step that lasts one frame is a twitch, and a body
;; that re-decides every tick never actually leaves the line of a swing.
(defn citizen-dodge-ms [] : I32 220)

;; Hurt enough to stop trading shots, but not hurt enough to abandon the fight: drop the profile and
;; give ground with the zombie still in front of you. 400 milli = 40 health.
(defn citizen-cover-health-pm [] : I32 400)
(defn citizen-cover-ms [] : I32 700)
;; Backpedal speed, milli of the shared MAX_SPEED path. Slow on purpose: cover is not flight, and a
;; body that moonwalks at full speed reads as a bug, not as caution.
(defn citizen-cover-backpedal-milli [] : I32 450)

;; Badly hurt: the fight is already lost, so it runs instead of trading. 250 milli = 25 health.
;; Deliberately BELOW citizen-cover-health-pm, so the three rungs are ordered: fight, cover, run.
(defn citizen-retreat-health-pm [] : I32 250)
(defn citizen-retreat-ms [] : I32 900)


;; ---- opinion 1: hand-written heuristics ------------------------------------------------------
;; Every scorer answers "how much does this action want to happen, 0..2000". `ready` is the host's
;; own jump/cooldown gate (1 = the body could jump right now), because "jump" is a legal *choice*
;; only when the body is able; the host still enforces it.

(defn citizen-idle-score [(dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)] : I32
  (if (= threat 0) 420 0))

(defn citizen-walk-score [(dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)] : I32
  (if (= threat 0) 900 (if (> dist 12000) 500 200)))

(defn citizen-run-score [(dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)] : I32
  (if (= threat 0) 260 (+ 380 (/ (citizen-clamp 0 20000 dist) 40))))

(defn citizen-jump-score [(dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)] : I32
  (if (= ready 0)
    0
    (if (and (= threat 1) (< dist 7000))
      (+ 600 (if (< health 400) 260 0))
      (if (= threat 0) 60 120))))

(defn citizen-crouch-score [(dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)] : I32
  (if (and (= threat 0) (< speed 200)) 240 0))

(defn citizen-slide-score [(dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)] : I32
  (if (and (= threat 1) (>= speed (citizen-slide-speed-milli)))
    (if (< dist 6000) 900 660)
    0))

(defn citizen-slide-jump-score [(dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)] : I32
  (if (and (= ready 1) (and (= threat 1) (and (>= speed (citizen-slide-speed-milli)) (< dist 5000))))
    980
    0))

;; Deliberately silent inside 2.5 m: a citizen that close is better off moving than aiming, and
;; without this floor the score ladder made shooting beat sliding at every range, which left the
;; founder's "slide at a zombie" unreachable no matter how fast the body was going.
(defn citizen-shoot-score [(dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)] : I32
  (if (and (= threat 1) (and (>= dist 2500) (< dist (citizen-fire-range-milli))))
    (+ 500 (/ (* (- (citizen-fire-range-milli) dist) 400) (citizen-fire-range-milli)))
    0))

(defn citizen-reload-score [(dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)] : I32
  (if (and (= threat 1) (< health 500) (> dist 6000)) 300 0))

;; A claw inside its reach outranks everything, including the trigger -- you cannot out-shoot a
;; swing that has already started. But a body ALREADY at sliding speed slides (the founder's own
;; move) rather than side-stepping, which is why the fast case is scored lower instead of higher:
;; 1500 standing still, 700 when the engine's own slide is the better answer.
(defn citizen-dodge-score [(dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)] : I32
  (if (and (= threat 1) (< dist (citizen-claw-reach-milli)))
    (if (< speed (citizen-slide-speed-milli)) 1500 700)
    0))

;; Hurt and close, but not yet being swung at: give ground with the gun still up. 900 is a rung
;; above a hurt jump (860) and above a shot at this range (about 760), and it deliberately stops at
;; 6 m -- past that a hurt citizen still jumps, which is what keeps the founder's own jump reachable
;; at all instead of cover swallowing every situation where the body is bleeding.
(defn citizen-cover-score [(dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)] : I32
  (if (and (= threat 1) (and (< health (citizen-cover-health-pm)) (< dist 6000)))
    900
    0))

;; The last rung. Outranks everything: a body at 25 health does not win a trade, it leaves.
(defn citizen-retreat-score [(dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)] : I32
  (if (and (= threat 1) (< health (citizen-retreat-health-pm))) 1400 0))

(defn citizen-heuristic-score
  [(action : I32) (dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)] : I32
  (if (= action 0) (citizen-idle-score dist threat health speed ready)
   (if (= action 1) (citizen-walk-score dist threat health speed ready)
    (if (= action 2) (citizen-run-score dist threat health speed ready)
     (if (= action 3) (citizen-jump-score dist threat health speed ready)
      (if (= action 4) (citizen-crouch-score dist threat health speed ready)
       (if (= action 5) (citizen-slide-score dist threat health speed ready)
        (if (= action 6) (citizen-slide-jump-score dist threat health speed ready)
         (if (= action 7) (citizen-shoot-score dist threat health speed ready)
          (if (= action 8) (citizen-reload-score dist threat health speed ready)
           (if (= action 9) (citizen-dodge-score dist threat health speed ready)
            (if (= action 10) (citizen-cover-score dist threat health speed ready)
             (if (= action 11) (citizen-retreat-score dist threat health speed ready)
              0)))))))))))))

;; ---- opinion 2: the hand-written policy ------------------------------------------------------
;; A six-input, one-output perceptron. Inputs are 0..1000 and the weights sum to 1000, so the output
;; is 0..1000 with no rescaling: 500 is "no strong feeling", 1000 is "deal with this NOW".
;;   proximity 320  -- how close the threat is (the dominant term, as it is in a real fight)
;;   hurt      260  -- low health makes a body decisive rather than careful
;;   threat    180  -- a hunting zombie is worth acting on at all
;;   ready     140  -- a body that cannot jump right now should not be scored as if it could
;;   speed      60  -- already moving is a small push toward committing
;;   ground     40  -- feet under you is a small push toward committing
;; These six weights are HAND WRITTEN, picked to be explainable, and not trained on anything. A
;; different set is a different citizen personality; the file is the tuning surface on purpose.
(defn citizen-policy-aggression
  [(proximity : I32) (hurt : I32) (threat : I32) (ready : I32) (speed : I32) (ground : I32)] : I32
  (citizen-clamp 0 1000
    (/ (+ (* (citizen-clamp 0 1000 proximity) 320)
          (* (citizen-clamp 0 1000 hurt) 260)
          (* (if (= threat 0) 0 1000) 180)
          (* (if (= ready 0) 0 1000) 140)
          (* (citizen-clamp 0 1000 speed) 60)
          (* (if (= ground 0) 0 1000) 40))
       1000)))

;; ---- mixing them -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; What each action gains or loses when the policy feels aggressive (aggression 500 = no change).
;; The policy never overrides the heuristics -- at full aggression a slide jumps +220 on a 2000
;; scale, which decides a close call and cannot beat a 720-vs-0 certainty. That ceiling is the point:
;; a hand-written net this small is a tie-breaker, not the driver.
(defn citizen-bias [(action : I32)] : I32
  (if (= action 0) -200
   (if (= action 1) -120
    (if (= action 2) 80
     (if (= action 3) 200
      (if (= action 4) 60
       (if (= action 5) 180
        (if (= action 6) 220
         (if (= action 7) 160
          (if (= action 8) 60
           (if (= action 9) 200
            (if (= action 10) 120
             (if (= action 11) 180 0)))))))))))))

(defn citizen-blended-score
  [(action : I32) (dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32)
   (aggression : I32)] : I32
  (citizen-clamp 0 2000
    (+ (citizen-heuristic-score action dist threat health speed ready)
       (/ (* (- aggression 500) (citizen-bias action)) 1000))))

;; The argmax. Ties go to the earlier action in the id order except that idle (0) is seeded with a
;; score of 0 and every action is compared with `>`, so a dead-flat field of zeroes still answers
;; "idle" -- a citizen with nothing to do stands still rather than twitching.
(defn citizen-pick
  [(dist : I32) (threat : I32) (health : I32) (speed : I32) (ready : I32) (aggression : I32)] : I32
  (loop [action 0 best -1 best-action 0]
    (if (>= action 12)
      best-action
      (let [score (citizen-blended-score action dist threat health speed ready aggression)]
        (if (> score best)
          (recur (+ action 1) score action)
          (recur (+ action 1) best best-action))))))
